  "note": "Election of three town commissioners in the Town Hall on Wednesday 15 January 1902. The outgoing members, Michael Smyth, J.P., Dr. Dorman and John Nugent (chairman), sought re-election, with John Hughes as a fourth candidate. Peter M'Knight, town clerk, returning officer; John Conroy, poll clerk. Nugent received 53 plumpers. The Irish News gives the same figures (its 185 for Smyth is faintly printed). No party labels are printed."
